        "original_id": "d6c47b7c-aa66-50c9-b68d-1dc8f94f1db7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Aberdeenshire, Scotland, Glasgow\n- People: Joan Kathleen Harding Eardley\n- Buildings: Fiddes Castle, Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, Muchalls Castle\n- Concepts: Scottish gothic style Palladian manor, prehistoric use, portraiture, landscapes, fishing village\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse that was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish gothic style Palladian manor.\n- Fetteresso Castle shows clear evidence of prehistoric use of its site.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- The general area around Catterline includes Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle as notable architectural or historic features.\n- Joan Kathleen Harding Eardley was a British artist born on 18 May 1921 and died on 16 August 1963.\n- Joan Kathleen Harding Eardley was noted for portraiture of street children in Glasgow and for landscapes of Catterline and its surroundings on Scotland's north-east coast.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
